{"vid":"K0xYMBmdUsI","source":"K0xYMBmdUsI.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"Stop pronouncing"},{"t":2.2,"txt":"this letter in English. Yep, the letter"},{"t":5.2,"txt":"R. The way you pronounce this letter"},{"t":9.3,"txt":"here can tell me"},{"t":11.7,"txt":"so much about your accent. In British"},{"t":14.9,"txt":"English,"},{"t":16.2,"txt":"we hardly ever pronounce it. Today, I'm"},{"t":19.8,"txt":"going to teach you when we never"},{"t":22.8,"txt":"pronounce the letter R, and I will also"},{"t":25.6,"txt":"show you when and why we do pronounce"},{"t":29,"txt":"it, including some examples of where you"},{"t":32,"txt":"may least expect it."},{"t":34.6,"txt":"Sometimes it's not even written, but we"},{"t":37.9,"txt":"still pronounce the R. Now, this is a"},{"t":41.2,"txt":"complex topic, but it's going to have a"},{"t":43.7,"txt":"big impact on your speaking and"},{"t":45.8,"txt":"pronunciation. To help you, we will go"},{"t":48.5,"txt":"through lots of examples and shadowing"},{"t":51.6,"txt":"tasks together for you to practice."},{"t":54.2,"txt":"Remember that shadowing means speaking"},{"t":56.6,"txt":"with me or speaking just after me. But"},{"t":60.4,"txt":"if you prefer, use the pause button and"},{"t":62.8,"txt":"just listen and repeat. Now, the silent"},{"t":65.3,"txt":"R, our topic today, is one of those"},{"t":67.9,"txt":"little details that can make a huge"},{"t":70.7,"txt":"difference in how natural your British"},{"t":73.2,"txt":"accent sounds. But this is just one"},{"t":75.9,"txt":"piece of the puzzle. There are a few"},{"t":78.1,"txt":"other key sounds and habits that can"},{"t":81.2,"txt":"make or break your British accent. You"},{"t":84.3,"txt":"can learn and perfect them in my 5-day"},{"t":87.6,"txt":"British accent boot camp. It's 5 days of"},{"t":91.2,"txt":"focused, practical training on vowel"},{"t":94.6,"txt":"sounds, the crisp t sound, British"},{"t":98.8,"txt":"vocabulary. It's all focused on modern"},{"t":102.5,"txt":"RP, which is my accent. My students say"},{"t":105.6,"txt":"they feel more confident and sound more"},{"t":107.9,"txt":"natural from the very first lesson. So,"},{"t":110.8,"txt":"imagine what you can achieve in 5 days."},{"t":113.7,"txt":"Right now, I'm offering lifetime access"},{"t":116.8,"txt":"and a huge discount. To learn more and"},{"t":120.4,"txt":"join, just click on the link in the"},{"t":122.4,"txt":"description or scan the QR code on"},{"t":125.2,"txt":"screen here. Let's get started with the"},{"t":127.6,"txt":"lesson. In my modern received"},{"t":129.9,"txt":"pronunciation accent, the letter R is"},{"t":133.4,"txt":"only pronounced when it comes before a"},{"t":136.5,"txt":"vowel sound. So, when you see an R"},{"t":139.3,"txt":"before a consonant sound or at the end"},{"t":142.6,"txt":"of a word with no sounds after it,"},{"t":145.8,"txt":"simply don't try to pronounce it. Here"},{"t":149,"txt":"are some examples. Repeat after me."},{"t":152.7,"txt":"earth"},{"t":155.8,"txt":"warmth"},{"t":159.6,"txt":"garden"},{"t":161.8,"txt":"There is no r sound in them. earth,"},{"t":165.9,"txt":"warmth, garden. In these words, the"},{"t":169.1,"txt":"letter R is followed by a consonant"},{"t":171.3,"txt":"sound, so it isn't pronounced. It's"},{"t":174.2,"txt":"silent. In stressed syllables like this,"},{"t":177.2,"txt":"we just pronounce the long vowel sounds"},{"t":180.9,"txt":"uh as in earth,"},{"t":183.6,"txt":"or as in warmth, and ar as in garden."},{"t":189.8,"txt":"The letter R is completely silent. In"},{"t":193.3,"txt":"the words water,"},{"t":195.5,"txt":"nature, and together, there is no sound"},{"t":200.2,"txt":"after the letter R, so we don't need to"},{"t":203.2,"txt":"make a r sound. Because the R is silent,"},{"t":207.9,"txt":"these words end with the uh vowel sound,"},{"t":211.5,"txt":"the schwa. This is a weak vowel sound."},{"t":215,"txt":"Notice how it appears in the unstressed"},{"t":217.8,"txt":"syllables in these words. Repeat after"},{"t":220.8,"txt":"me."},{"t":221.9,"txt":"water"},{"t":224.8,"txt":"nature"},{"t":227.7,"txt":"together"},{"t":230.1,"txt":"Let's practice the silent R now. Shadow"},{"t":233,"txt":"me if you can, or listen and repeat"},{"t":235.6,"txt":"after me. I'll put the silent R's in red"},{"t":239.3,"txt":"to help you. My garden has a quiet"},{"t":242.5,"txt":"corner."},{"t":243.8,"txt":"I go there to clear my mind when I'm"},{"t":246.9,"txt":"tense, tired, or nervous."},{"t":253.1,"txt":"A lot of my students try to pronounce"},{"t":255.6,"txt":"the R in tired and say something like"},{"t":259.8,"txt":"tired."},{"t":261.4,"txt":"Forget the R, just say tired."},{"t":266.1,"txt":"Tired."},{"t":267.8,"txt":"Hear how much smoother that sounds?"},{"t":270.5,"txt":"Tired. Accents that follow this silent R"},{"t":274.7,"txt":"rule are called non-rhotic accents. My"},{"t":279.3,"txt":"modern RP accent and most, but not all,"},{"t":283.5,"txt":"British accents are non-rhotic. This is"},{"t":287.2,"txt":"not the case in North America. Most"},{"t":291,"txt":"accents there pronounce the R in all"},{"t":294.7,"txt":"positions, before consonant sounds and"},{"t":298.1,"txt":"at the end of words. I think it's really"},{"t":300.2,"txt":"good for you to hear the difference. So,"},{"t":302.5,"txt":"let's hear a general American version of"},{"t":306,"txt":"the same sentence to compare."},{"t":308.4,"txt":">> My garden has a quiet corner. I go there"},{"t":311.5,"txt":"to clear my mind when I'm tense, tired,"},{"t":314.3,"txt":"or nervous."},{"t":315.2,"txt":">> There's a pretty big difference, right?"},{"t":317.9,"txt":"The silent R is one of the main features"},{"t":320.7,"txt":"that distinguishes British pronunciation"},{"t":323.6,"txt":"from American pronunciation. Now, in"},{"t":326.6,"txt":"both rhotic and non-rhotic accents, the"},{"t":330.2,"txt":"letter R is always pronounced before"},{"t":333.1,"txt":"vowel sounds at the beginning of words,"},{"t":336.2,"txt":"as in restful, relax, and reflect. It is"},{"t":342,"txt":"also pronounced within words, like"},{"t":345.6,"txt":"breathe,"},{"t":347,"txt":"serene,"},{"t":348.5,"txt":"and grounded."},{"t":350.9,"txt":"Let's practice now with a mixture of"},{"t":353.4,"txt":"silent and pronounced r's. Shadow me if"},{"t":358.5,"txt":"you can. The silent r's are red and in"},{"t":362.2,"txt":"bold."},{"t":363.4,"txt":"The pronounced r's are in green. Ready?"},{"t":367.9,"txt":"I feel much more serene and relaxed when"},{"t":372.3,"txt":"I take deep breaths."},{"t":375.2,"txt":"The rich smell of the earth and sound of"},{"t":378.5,"txt":"running water help me to stay grounded."},{"t":385.6,"txt":"Now, I know I said we always pronounce"},{"t":389.2,"txt":"the letter r before vowel sounds, but"},{"t":392.2,"txt":"this is a very dangerous thing to say"},{"t":395,"txt":"because in English there are always"},{"t":397.5,"txt":"exceptions. One very common exception"},{"t":401.2,"txt":"is this word here."},{"t":403.7,"txt":"How do you pronounce it? If we follow"},{"t":407,"txt":"the rules, they state that it should be"},{"t":410,"txt":"pronounced iron because the letter r is"},{"t":413.5,"txt":"followed by the vowel sound uh."},{"t":416.5,"txt":"But, the letter r is never pronounced in"},{"t":419.8,"txt":"this word."},{"t":421.5,"txt":"It's an exception. It always catches my"},{"t":424.9,"txt":"students out. It should be pronounced"},{"t":428.1,"txt":"iron."},{"t":429.7,"txt":"Iron. Some examples are I love Iron"},{"t":433.4,"txt":"Maiden or I'm competing in an Iron Man"},{"t":437.7,"txt":"next month."},{"t":439.4,"txt":"Not Iron Maiden, not Iron Man."},{"t":442.7,"txt":"Iron. Remember, I'm modeling my accent"},{"t":445.4,"txt":"here. In a North American accent, these"},{"t":448.5,"txt":"words could sound more like this."},{"t":451.8,"txt":">> I love Iron Maiden."},{"t":454.2,"txt":"I'm competing in an Iron Man next month."},{"t":457.3,"txt":">> And I have a few more exceptions for"},{"t":459.3,"txt":"you. In English, we often drop syllables"},{"t":462.5,"txt":"in the middle of words, and when we do,"},{"t":465.2,"txt":"the letter R can sometimes disappear."},{"t":468.5,"txt":"Even when technically it should be"},{"t":471,"txt":"pronounced. For example, the first R in"},{"t":475.2,"txt":"this word, February,"},{"t":477.8,"txt":"often disappears and we tend to say"},{"t":481.2,"txt":"February."},{"t":482.5,"txt":"I favor February. That's how I was"},{"t":485.3,"txt":"taught to say it. The first R in this"},{"t":488.2,"txt":"word,"},{"t":489.8,"txt":"library,"},{"t":491.9,"txt":"library, often disappears, too, and we"},{"t":495.3,"txt":"say library. Again, I favor the dropped"},{"t":499.5,"txt":"version, library. So, to recap, never"},{"t":503.2,"txt":"pronounce the letter R when it comes"},{"t":505.2,"txt":"before a consonant sound or at the end"},{"t":507.6,"txt":"of a word."},{"t":508.9,"txt":"Only pronounce the letter R when it's"},{"t":511.3,"txt":"followed by a vowel sound. This rule is"},{"t":513.8,"txt":"true in connected speech, too. Notice"},{"t":516.9,"txt":"how my pronunciation changes when R"},{"t":520.1,"txt":"comes at the end of a word,"},{"t":523,"txt":"at the end of a word, then followed by a"},{"t":525.8,"txt":"consonant sound, and at the end of a"},{"t":528.3,"txt":"word followed by a vowel sound. Clear."},{"t":533.5,"txt":"Clear mind."},{"t":535.9,"txt":"Clearer."},{"t":538.6,"txt":"Better."},{"t":540,"txt":"Better sleep."},{"t":542.3,"txt":"Better atmosphere."},{"t":545.2,"txt":"Here."},{"t":546.8,"txt":"Here now."},{"t":549,"txt":"Here and now."},{"t":551,"txt":"Your."},{"t":552.6,"txt":"Your peace."},{"t":555,"txt":"Your inner peace. This is called a"},{"t":558.1,"txt":"linking R. Adding a linking R sound"},{"t":561.6,"txt":"before vowel sounds isn't obligatory,"},{"t":564.6,"txt":"but it can help us to glide between the"},{"t":567.2,"txt":"vowel sounds more easily."},{"t":569.5,"txt":"Think of it as a little bridge between"},{"t":572,"txt":"vowel sounds."},{"t":573.5,"txt":"Okay, let's practice everything we've"},{"t":575.3,"txt":"learned so far. Shadow me now. I've"},{"t":578.3,"txt":"marked the silent, pronounced, and"},{"t":580.9,"txt":"linking R's to help. I wander slowly"},{"t":584.3,"txt":"through the garden listening to the tree"},{"t":587.5,"txt":"leaves rustling in the warm afternoon"},{"t":590.6,"txt":"breeze. I focus on the here and now and"},{"t":594.8,"txt":"appreciate the simpler approach to life."},{"t":601.2,"txt":"Okay, so now we know when and when not"},{"t":604.3,"txt":"to pronounce the letter R when we see it"},{"t":606.8,"txt":"written."},{"t":608,"txt":"But, at the beginning of the lesson, I"},{"t":610.6,"txt":"promised that I'd tell you about a time"},{"t":613.2,"txt":"we pronounce the letter R that might"},{"t":615.9,"txt":"surprise you."},{"t":617.5,"txt":"Well, here it is."},{"t":619.8,"txt":"Listen and repeat these phrases with me."},{"t":623.5,"txt":"What do you notice?"},{"t":625.9,"txt":"Idea of calm."},{"t":630.2,"txt":"Law of nature."},{"t":633.6,"txt":"Spa experience."},{"t":636.8,"txt":"That's right. I added an er sound even"},{"t":641.4,"txt":"though there is no written R at all. We"},{"t":644.4,"txt":"can add an er sound in phrases like this"},{"t":648.5,"txt":"when a word ends in a"},{"t":651.4,"txt":"or and a and the next word begins with a"},{"t":655.9,"txt":"vowel sound."},{"t":657.5,"txt":"This is called the intrusive R and is a"},{"t":660.4,"txt":"really common feature of British"},{"t":662.6,"txt":"English. Not everyone does it, but I do"},{"t":666,"txt":"it sometimes."},{"t":667.4,"txt":"Let's practice together. Shadow me now."},{"t":669.9,"txt":"I was halfway through our cinema evening"},{"t":673.8,"txt":"when I saw it clearly. I needed to go on"},{"t":677.3,"txt":"a yoga and meditation retreat surrounded"},{"t":681.2,"txt":"by flora and fauna in an area of peace"},{"t":684.7,"txt":"and quiet."},{"t":688.8,"txt":"Ooh."},{"t":689.9,"txt":"That's challenging. It can feel forced."},{"t":693.3,"txt":"Only do it if it feels natural to you."},{"t":696.6,"txt":"If I think about it too hard, it sounds"},{"t":699.6,"txt":"really weird, but it does come out"},{"t":701.2,"txt":"naturally for me. Now, this can happen"},{"t":703.9,"txt":"within words, too. So, you might hear an"},{"t":707.8,"txt":"er sound in words with no written r. For"},{"t":711.6,"txt":"example, drawing and soaring."},{"t":716.7,"txt":"You can pronounce them drawing and"},{"t":718.7,"txt":"soaring or drawing and soaring. Right,"},{"t":722.8,"txt":"that brings us to the end of today's"},{"t":724.8,"txt":"video lesson. I really hope you've"},{"t":726.7,"txt":"enjoyed practicing with me. And if you"},{"t":729.2,"txt":"want to keep on improving your British"},{"t":731.2,"txt":"accent, don't forget to check out my"},{"t":733.5,"txt":"5-day British accent boot camp. It is"},{"t":736.8,"txt":"packed with focused lessons to help you"},{"t":739.8,"txt":"sound more natural and confident."},{"t":743,"txt":"The link is in the description box or"},{"t":745.1,"txt":"you can scan the QR code there. I will"},{"t":747.1,"txt":"see you in the next video. Bye."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"Stop"},{"t":0.76,"w":"pronouncing"},{"t":2.24,"w":"this"},{"t":2.6,"w":"letter"},{"t":3.44,"w":"in"},{"t":3.6,"w":"English."},{"t":4.16,"w":"Yep,"},{"t":4.68,"w":"the"},{"t":4.84,"w":"letter"},{"t":5.2,"w":"R."},{"t":6.04,"w":"The"},{"t":6.28,"w":"way"},{"t":6.76,"w":"you"},{"t":7.04,"w":"pronounce"},{"t":8.28,"w":"this"},{"t":8.8,"w":"letter"},{"t":9.28,"w":"here"},{"t":10.2,"w":"can"},{"t":10.4,"w":"tell"},{"t":10.72,"w":"me"},{"t":11.72,"w":"so"},{"t":12.04,"w":"much"},{"t":12.72,"w":"about"},{"t":13.12,"w":"your"},{"t":13.32,"w":"accent."},{"t":14.16,"w":"In"},{"t":14.4,"w":"British"},{"t":14.92,"w":"English,"},{"t":16.2,"w":"we"},{"t":16.6,"w":"hardly"},{"t":17.2,"w":"ever"},{"t":17.56,"w":"pronounce"},{"t":18.2,"w":"it."},{"t":18.88,"w":"Today,"},{"t":19.52,"w":"I'm"},{"t":19.76,"w":"going"},{"t":19.96,"w":"to"},{"t":